.TH ONYM 1 2026-06-22 "Onym 0.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
onym \- thesaurus and dictionary for GNOME built on Open English WordNet
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B onym
.RI [ word ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Onym
is a thesaurus and dictionary for GNOME, built on Open English WordNet. It
shows a word's meanings grouped by part of speech, with example sentences, then
its synonyms, its antonyms, and the lexical relations that connect it to other
words. Where they are known, it also shows a word's etymology and the words
other languages use for each sense. Every word on screen is a link, so one
lookup leads to the next with a click. Search is live, with completion as you
type and a suggestion when a word is misspelt.
.PP
With no argument, Onym opens to its search field. Given a
.IR word ,
it opens showing that word.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WNSEARCHDIR
The directory holding the word database. When it is unset, Onym falls back to
.IR $WNHOME/dict ,
then to the directory chosen at build time.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I (build-time data directory)
The word database: the Open English WordNet base and its etymology and
translation overlays, prepared from the bundled onym-data project. The location
is fixed at build time and is overridden by
.B WNSEARCHDIR
above. There is no system WordNet fallback.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wn (1)
.SH AUTHOR
ursa.nz <code@ursa.nz>
